A||N||7||Smokin' GT||What kind of paint to use on valve covers & top of intake manifold? (pics of colors?)||||5||
Z||000000||Smokin' GT||10-28-2001||04:01 AM||||That's basically the question, I've seen someone do it with "electron blue" and it looked awesome, but I'm not sure if I have to use high temp paint (engine or caliper paint?) or powder coating or what.  So if you guys have any suggestions of what to use or have some pics of some different colors you guys have used it would be very helpful. Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||07:14 AM||||Do a search for engine pics or plenum pics, or whatever. Just make sure the old paint is all off and the parts prepped right to prevent flaking.  There are a lot of casting marks, etc which can be ground off the plenum to smooth it up.  The cheapest route would be a high temp engine paint although if you wanted to powder coat or polish it's up to you.  Have fun!<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian87egotrip||10-28-2001||08:43 AM||||I did my valve cover and intake with the same paint my car was painted with. PPG is the brand. I have had no problems with it at all, I drive my car every day. The heat has not effected it, been about 2.5 years now.   <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-28-2001||01:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brian87egotrip:<BR><B>I did my valve cover and intake with the same paint my car was painted with.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same here!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||10-28-2001||03:05 PM||||OK, if you insist...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/pffengine2.jpg"> <P>Powdercoated. I think you can get equal results by using Dupli-Color ceramic engine paint. Chrysler red is the match for the factory color, or use your imagination.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTDusty||10-28-2001||10:53 PM|||| I just rough sanded mine and used several coats of High-temp engine paint and then several coats of high temp clear. Looks show-room shiny!<P>Dusty||||reg||10
